\ auc ( outcomes scores -- f ), brier ( outcomes probabilities -- f ),
\ complete-cases ( xs ys -- xs' ys' ): ROC AUC = P(a random positive scores
\ above a random negative), ties counted half and so order-independent, NaN
\ scores dropping their row, both classes required; Brier mean squared error,
\ NaN-skipping; and paired complete-case filtering.

\ === auc: basic ordering ===
[ 1 1 0 ] 3 1 matrix  [ 3 1 2 ] 3 1 matrix  auc . cr        \ 0.5
[ 1 0 ] 2 1 matrix    [ 2 1 ] 2 1 matrix    auc . cr        \ 1
[ 1 0 ] 2 1 matrix    [ 1 2 ] 2 1 matrix    auc . cr        \ 0
[ 0 0 1 1 ] 4 1 matrix  [ 1 2 3 4 ] 4 1 matrix  auc . cr    \ 1 (perfect)

\ === auc: ties counted half; equal scores give 0.5 in any row order ===
[ 1 0 ] 2 1 matrix      [ 2 2 ] 2 1 matrix        auc . cr  \ 0.5 (one cross-class tie)
[ 1 1 0 0 ] 4 1 matrix  [ 5 5 5 5 ] 4 1 matrix    auc . cr  \ 0.5 (all tied)
[ 0 1 0 1 ] 4 1 matrix  [ 5 5 5 5 ] 4 1 matrix    auc . cr  \ 0.5 (same, reordered)

\ === auc: a NaN score drops its row, outcomes stay aligned ===
[ 1 1 0 ] 3 1 matrix  [ 3 nan 2 ] 3 1 matrix  auc . cr      \ 1 (row 2 dropped -> pos{3} neg{2})

\ === brier: mean squared error, NaN elements skipped ===
[ 1 1 0 ] 3 1 matrix  [ 3 1 2 ] 3 1 matrix     brier . cr   \ 2.66667
[ 1 0 ] 2 1 matrix    [ 0.9 0.1 ] 2 1 matrix   brier . cr   \ 0.01
[ 1 1 0 ] 3 1 matrix  [ 0.8 nan 0.2 ] 3 1 matrix brier . cr \ 0.04 (NaN skipped)

\ === complete-cases: drop paired NaN rows, aligned ===
[ 1 nan 2 ] 3 1 matrix  [ 4 5 6 ] 3 1 matrix  complete-cases . cr . cr

\ === errors (reason parenthesized) ===
[ 1 1 ] 2 1 matrix  [ 3 1 ] 2 1 matrix  auc                 \ (single class: no negative)
